Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:49:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: binance_reconcile_fetch query_symbols accepts a
 callable (v0.13.1) (#6)

* feat: binance_reconcile_fetch query_symbols accepts a callable(position_rows) (v0.13.1)

Task 3 L3, needed by momentum's adapter (PR-3).  momentum's reconcile fill
window is "the open positions' symbols unioned with a static RECONCILE_SYMBOLS
env list", and the positions are only known after they are fetched.

BinanceReconcileParams.query_symbols now also accepts
Callable[[list[dict]], Sequence[str]] -- invoked after the positions section
with the normalized (ledger-form) position rows, returning the native symbols
to pull user_trades for.  A plain sequence still works unchanged (seykota).
If the positions section fails the callable gets [] (the static env list is
still included by momentum's callable).

_fill_rows takes the resolved list explicitly; new _resolve_query_symbols
helper.  Backward compatible.  +2 tests (112).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* docs: note that a query_symbols callable's exception is not caught (per PR #6 review)

Non-blocking suggestion from the Perplexity PASS on PR #6: make explicit in the
docstrings that a callable query_symbols propagates its own exception out of
fetch()/run() -- deliberate (adapter bug should fail loudly, not be swallowed
like a flaky exchange call).  Docstring-only, no logic change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

